  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Mark",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 12,
    "summary": "Jesus gives the parable of the wicked husbandmen—He speaks of paying taxes, celestial marriage, the two great commandments, the divine sonship of Christ, and the widow’s mites.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And he began to speak unto them by parables. A certain man planted a vineyard, and set an hedge about it, and digged a place for the winefat, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 54
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 105
          },
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 128
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:1",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And at the season he sent to the husbandmen a servant, that he might receive from the husbandmen of the fruit of the vineyard.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:2",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And they caught him, and beat him, and sent him away empty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:3",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And again he sent unto them another servant; and at him they cast stones, and wounded him in the head, and sent him away shamefully handled.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 89
          },
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 115
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:4",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And again he sent another; and him they killed, and many others; beating some, and killing some.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:5",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Having yet therefore one son, his wellbeloved, he sent him also last unto them, saying, They will reverence my son.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:6",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "But those husbandmen said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and the inheritance shall be ours.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:7",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And they took him, and killed him, and cast him out of the vineyard.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 34
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mark 12:8",
        "book": "Mark",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "What shall therefore the lord of the vineyard do? he will come and destroy the husbandmen, and will give the vineyard unto others.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "TG Vineyard of the Lord."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
